<title>USA: Worker killed at Howell Corp plant.</title>
<headline>Worker killed at Howell Corp plant.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>One worker died and two others were injured on Thursday when the fuel tank they were cleaning at a Howell Corp chemical plant here exploded, officials said.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement the cause of the explosion was under investigation.</p>
<p>It said the two surviving workers had been hospitalized with &quot;serious&quot; injuries. The workers were in the final stages of cleaning the tank, which had been used to store fuel oil, when the explosion occurred.</p>
<p>Damage was limited to the storage tank, the statement said.</p>
</text>
